Z||000000||Mach10||08-20-2001||05:11 AM||||Went out to the Sunday Nite Cruise on Portage with Baldlobo. He witnessed each one. Tonight, Bunsen Burner is undefeated:<P>1)Late 80s Monte Carlo SS. 1/2-3/4 car lengths  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>2)late model Anal Probe GT Monte was ahead <BR>of him, I was ahead of Monte. 1-1'1/2 lengths<P>3)Chevy Cavalier. No contest. Multiple car lengths. He made some neato squeeling noises, though... Little punk &gt;:|<P>4)Heavily riced out Accord or Civic. Couldn't tell. Had all sorts of gauges. Didn't help him none  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> 1/2-3/4 lengths<P>5)Mid-late 80s Camaro R/S. Same pack as Honda. Was about even with honda. 1/2-3/4 lengths<P>Not bad for an evening, huh? I'm beggining to think that the Auto v-6s are sadly underestimated  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> I was surprised as hell to mash that SS, though. I think it was mostly driver skill. I.E., he had none. He wasted way too much time burning out. Then again, he couldn't catch me either, until I shut 'er down. Funny, I thought I was only racing the Anal Probe. That's when the SS started spitting rubber. 3-way race. Almost empty street, to 80KPH. Fun times, and no boxes of Kittens  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||216.81.27.78||reg||6
